WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.612
Practice is the bridge between knowing about something and being able to do it.

00:00:04.612 --> 00:00:09.768
A learner may understand an explanation and still struggle when asked to perform the task independently.

00:00:09.768 --> 00:00:11.057
That gap is normal.

00:00:11.057 --> 00:00:14.601
Performance grows when learners see examples, try guided exercises, make decisions,

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:17.824
receive feedback, correct mistakes, and repeat the work with variation.

00:00:17.824 --> 00:00:20.080
Practice turns abstract understanding into usable skill.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.980
Deliberate practice is focused practice with a clear target.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.558
It is not repeating easy tasks on autopilot.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:29.747
It asks the learner to work on a specific capability, notice the result,

00:00:29.747 --> 00:00:30.397
and adjust.

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:35.553
Worked examples help early in learning because they show how an experienced person approaches the task.

00:00:35.553 --> 00:00:39.420
Guided exercises then let learners complete part of the work with support.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:40.709
Independent application comes later,

00:00:40.709 --> 00:00:44.254
when learners are ready to make more of the decisions themselves.

00:00:44.254 --> 00:00:47.155
Feedback is most useful when it helps learners improve,

00:00:47.155 --> 00:00:49.088
not merely when it judges them.

00:00:49.088 --> 00:00:51.666
A score can tell someone how they did,

00:00:51.666 --> 00:00:54.889
but specific feedback tells them what to adjust and why.

00:00:54.889 --> 00:00:58.756
Timely feedback is easier to connect to the action that produced it.

00:00:58.756 --> 00:01:02.623
Corrective feedback should be clear, respectful, and tied to the performance goal.

00:01:02.623 --> 00:01:05.201
The message is not simply, that was wrong.

00:01:05.201 --> 00:01:06.167
The message is,

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:10.035
here is the difference between the current approach and the stronger approach,

00:01:10.035 --> 00:01:12.613
and here is how to close the gap.

00:01:12.613 --> 00:01:14.868
Variation keeps practice from becoming memorized theater.

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:19.058
If every exercise uses the same wording, same order, and same obvious clue,

00:01:19.058 --> 00:01:22.280
learners may pass the activity without recognizing the idea elsewhere.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:23.247
Changing examples, constraints,

00:01:23.247 --> 00:01:27.114
or decision points helps learners separate the underlying principle from the surface

00:01:27.114 --> 00:01:28.725
features of the practice item.

00:01:28.725 --> 00:01:31.620
That is where practice begins to support real skill.
